v0.097: fix build_exe.bat PyInstaller PATH failure

- build_exe.bat called the bare "pyinstaller" command, which isn't on PATH
  on most Windows Python installs even when the package installed fine
  (pip puts its .exe in Python's Scripts folder, not the main install dir).
  Switched to "python -m PyInstaller", which works regardless of PATH.
- Added upfront checks (python present, PyInstaller present - installing
  requirements.txt automatically if not) and errorlevel checks after each
  step, so a real failure stops with a clear message instead of printing
  a misleading "Done - see dist\BNSPrintAgent.exe".
- Documented the gotcha in print-agent/README.md's troubleshooting section.

